Relevant columns and potential usage  
1. SAMPLE_COMMITS."repo_name": join‑key with LANGUAGES to know the repository of every commit record.  
2. SAMPLE_COMMITS."author": VARIANT holding an object with member "date" (epoch‑microseconds) → extract commit time.  
3. LANGUAGES."repo_name": join‑key with SAMPLE_COMMITS.  
4. LANGUAGES."language": VARIANT; look for the string “Python” to filter repos that contain Python code.

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each returns ≤ 20 rows, all identifiers quoted) that gradually build up the logic needed to calculate the average number of commits per month made in 2016 by repositories that contain Python code.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at the languages table to understand how languages are stored.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "language"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Find distinct repositories whose language list contains the word “Python”.
SELECT DISTINCT
  "repo_name"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES
WHERE CAST("language" AS STRING) ILIKE '%Python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Look at the commit table structure and raw author payload.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "commit",
  "author"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Extract author‑side epoch‑microsecond timestamps to verify the numeric format.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "commit",
  "author":"date"::NUMBER          AS "author_date_micro",
  "author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000 AS "author_date_sec"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Convert the epoch‑seconds into Snowflake TIMESTAMP for human readability.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "commit",
  TO_TIMESTAMP("author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000) AS "author_ts"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) List a few commits from repositories that do contain Python.
SELECT 
  c."repo_name",
  c."commit",
  TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000) AS "author_ts"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS c
JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES l
      ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE CAST(l."language" AS STRING) ILIKE '%Python%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Restrict to commits whose author date falls in calendar year 2016.
SELECT 
  c."repo_name",
  c."commit",
  TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000) AS "author_ts"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS c
WHERE DATE_TRUNC('year', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000)) = '2016-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Combine Python‑repos filter with 2016‑year filter.
SELECT
  c."repo_name",
  c."commit",
  TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000) AS "author_ts"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS c
JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES l
      ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE CAST(l."language" AS STRING) ILIKE '%Python%'
  AND DATE_TRUNC('year', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000)) = '2016-01-01'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Aggregate—count commits per repo per month in 2016 for Python repositories.
SELECT
  c."repo_name",
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000)) AS "month_2016",
  COUNT(*)                                                            AS "commit_cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS c
JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES l
      ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
WHERE CAST(l."language" AS STRING) ILIKE '%Python%'
  AND DATE_TRUNC('year', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000)) = '2016-01-01'
GROUP BY
  c."repo_name",
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000))
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Compute the average number of commits per month across all Python repositories in 2016.
SELECT
  AVG(monthly_cnt) AS "avg_commits_per_month_2016"
FROM (
  SELECT
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000)) AS "month_2016",
    COUNT(*)                                                               AS "monthly_cnt"
  FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_COMMITS c
  JOIN GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.LANGUAGES l
        ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
  WHERE CAST(l."language" AS STRING) ILIKE '%Python%'
    AND DATE_TRUNC('year', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000)) = '2016-01-01'
  GROUP BY
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP(c."author":"date"::NUMBER / 1000000))
)
LIMIT 20;
```

These queries illustrate all the pieces—language filtering, commit‑time extraction, 2016 selection, grouping by month, and averaging—needed to answer “average commits per month in 2016 for repositories containing Python code.”
